<title>BELGIUM: EU' sees no quick decision on BA/AMR alliance.</title>
<headline>EU' sees no quick decision on BA/AMR alliance.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>European competition commissioner Karel Van Miert said on Tuesday that the Commission was unlikely to rule on the alliance between British Airways and American Airlines before the end of August.</p>
<p>&quot;This is certainly going beyond the summer break,&quot; Van Miert told reporters as he arrived for a conference.</p>
<p>Replying to questions about a meeting on Monday with BA chairman Robert Ayling, Van Miert said the talks had been &quot;constructive.&quot;</p>
<p>But because the Commission would have to consult a committee of national competition officials on the alliance, a final recommendation was unlikely to be adopted before the Commission broke for its summer recess in August.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6830</p>
